2.0.1:

-- Event Data Architecture --

[Change] Rename events.dat to pressure.dat; honest naming for the pressure
      scoring workspace which is pruned every ~10 half-lives (~50 min) and
      serves only the exponential-decay pressure model
[New] Write observed (sub-trip) auth failure events to attack.pool with
      ACTION=observed; all detected IPs now recorded, not just ban-triggering
[New] events_list, events_list_ip, events_list_cidr functions backed by
      attack.pool; dashboard shows all IPs with sortable/filterable event
      history, IP detail shows durable failure counts + live pressure + log
      sample, CIDR search scans full retention window
[Change] _apool_awk: add sort_mode (count/time/ip), limit (0=unlimited),
      and CIDR filter params; backward compatible — defaults match prior
      behavior (count desc, limit 25, no CIDR)
[Change] Rewire -e|--events CLI to call events_list functions backed by
      attack.pool; event history now persists across pressure decay cycles
[New] Pre-parse flags --sort=count|time|ip, --24h, --7d, --30d for event
      list sorting and time window filtering
[Change] usage()/usage_short(): updated -e description and added new event
      modifier flags to output modifier sections

-- UAT Fixes --

[Fix] CLI: suppress version banner (vhead) for --json and --csv output in -l,
      -e, and -a handlers; structured data is no longer corrupted by banner text
[Fix] _apool_summary: read bans.active in the empty-attack-pool early-return
      path so Active Bans count is correct even when attack.pool is empty
[Fix] list_bans_json: output compact "[]" when no active bans instead of
      multi-line "[\n\n]"; matches events_dashboard_json empty format
[Fix] importconf: merge_conf() preserves original file permissions after awk
      rewrite; .tmp file inherited umask (022) making conf.bfd/internals.conf
      world-readable (644) instead of 640
[Fix] tests/Dockerfile: add missing COPY directives for README, CHANGELOG,
      COPYING.GPL, logrotate.d.bfd, bfd.timer required by install.sh
[Change] usage(): SIGHUP config reload hint added under -w/--watch entry
[Change] install.sh postinfo(): config reload command shown in post-install
      banner when watch mode is enabled or restarted

-- Alert Pressure Clarity --

[New] alert templates show failure count alongside pressure score: "N failed
      logins" in email (text/HTML), "(N failures)" in Slack/Telegram/Discord
[New] FAIL_COUNT template variable — actual failure count passed through alert
      pipeline as field 13; fallback to ceil(pressure/weight) for compatibility
[Change] conf.bfd and pressure.conf: added quick-reference comment translating
      pressure to failed logins (trip / weight = minimum rapid failures)
[Change] bfd.1 man page: added practical explanation to PRESSURE MODEL section;
      FAIL_COUNT listed in template variables
[Change] README.md: added quick-reference callout to pressure model section;
      FAIL_COUNT added to template variable table

[Change] update vendored tlog_lib.sh 2.0.2 to 2.0.3; adds inline error
      suppression comments and corrupt-archive stderr handling

[Fix] bfd: move config_loaded audit event to watch mode only (startup and
      SIGHUP reload); eliminates per-invocation audit/syslog noise from cron

-- Test Suite Optimization --

[Change] firewall-backend tests: converted 4 APF/CSF ban/unban subshell tests
      to direct function calls, eliminating redundant bfd.lib.sh re-sourcing
[Change] watch-mode tests: replaced fixed sleeps (sleep 0.5/1/2) with log-based
      polling loops (sleep 0.1 with grep checks), reducing worst-case wait time
[Change] config-validation tests: consolidated run_validate/run_validate_output
      into single _run_validate_impl helper with mode parameter
[Fix] removed 3 redundant valid-IP tests and 1 redundant invalid-IP test in
      01-validate-ip.bats (zero coverage loss)
[Fix] removed redundant pressure_format 15000 test in 30-pressure.bats (same
      code path as 1000 test)

-- QA Integration Fixes --

[Fix] bfd_alert.sh: _bfd_dispatch_messaging now passes entry_num and
      entry_total to _alert_set_entry_vars, matching the correct 4-argument
      call pattern used by _alert_render_text/_alert_render_html
[Fix] bfd: elog_output_enable "stdout" added after elog_init so eout()
      echoes to stdout as expected by the eout() contract
[Change] bfd: inline comments clarified on elog_output_enable suppression
      explaining why 2>/dev/null || true is safe
[Change] vendored elog_lib.sh updated from v1.0.0 to v1.0.2 (ELOG_AUDIT_FILE
      expansion fix for non-root)
[Change] vendored alert_lib.sh updated from v1.0.0 to v1.0.3 (sed injection
      fix in _alert_slack_post_message, QA fixes)
[Change] vendored pkg_lib.sh updated from v1.0.0 to v1.0.1 (pkg_sed_replace
      delimiter escaping fix, QA fixes)

-- pkg_lib Integration Fixes --

[Fix] install.sh: PKG_BACKUP_SYMLINK set to "bfd.bk.last" before sourcing
      pkg_lib so backup symlink matches importconf expectations; upgrade
      detection uses pkg_backup_exists/pkg_backup_path instead of direct
      directory test
[Fix] importconf: BK_LAST variable with fallback to legacy symlink path;
      all backup references use $BK_LAST for correct path resolution when
      invoked by install.sh via pkg_backup_path()
[Fix] install.sh: systemd unit sed replacement uses _pkg_systemd_unit_dir()
      auto-detected path instead of hardcoded /etc/systemd/system/; prevents
      sed targeting wrong directory on RHEL/Debian where units install to
      /usr/lib/systemd/system/ or /lib/systemd/system/
[Fix] install.sh/uninstall.sh: legacy /etc/systemd/system/ units cleaned on
      upgrade and uninstall to prevent systemd priority conflict with units
      in auto-detected directory
[Fix] uninstall.sh: backup glob widened to match both old (.bk.*) and new
      pkg_lib (.TIMESTAMP) naming formats

-- pkg_lib Integration --

[New] pkg_lib.sh v1.0.0 integrated as shared packaging/installer library at
      files/internals/pkg_lib.sh; provides standardized backup, file operations,
      service lifecycle, cron management, man page, and uninstall primitives
[Change] install.sh refactored to use pkg_lib functions: pkg_backup, pkg_copy_tree,
      pkg_set_perms, pkg_create_dirs, pkg_symlink, pkg_logrotate_install,
      pkg_man_install (now gzips man pages), pkg_bash_completion, pkg_cron_install,
      pkg_cron_preserve_schedule/pkg_cron_restore_schedule, pkg_service_install_multi,
      pkg_sed_replace, pkg_header/pkg_section/pkg_success/pkg_item for output
[Change] uninstall.sh refactored to use pkg_lib functions: pkg_uninstall_confirm,
      pkg_service_uninstall, pkg_uninstall_man, pkg_uninstall_completion,
      pkg_uninstall_logrotate, pkg_uninstall_cron, pkg_uninstall_files
[New] pkg.manifest project metadata file for pkg_gen.sh template generation

-- Rule Coverage Expansion --

[Change] README.md and bfd.1 man page: rule count updated from 42 to 47;
      rule catalog table expanded with cockpit, postscreen, gitea, nextcloud,
      interworx
[New] cpanel rule: cPanel 76+ log format pattern; webmail ports 2095,2096
[New] interworx rule: NodeWorx/SiteWorx login failure pattern; weight=5/trip=10
      (panel tier); port 2443; log-file-detected PREREQ
[Change] plesk rule: PREREQ fallback for Debian/Ubuntu /opt/psa path
[New] gitea rule: 2 patterns for Gitea/Forgejo self-hosted Git (Failed
      authentication attempt, invalid credentials); weight=2/trip=10; port 3000;
      cascading PREREQ fallback for gitea and forgejo binary paths
[New] nextcloud rule: 2 patterns for Nextcloud file sync (Login failed, Trusted
      domain error); weight=2/trip=10; ports 80,443; log-file-detected PREREQ
[New] cockpit rule: 3 patterns for Cockpit web console (pam_unix, cockpit-ws,
      cockpit-session); weight=5/trip=10 (panel tier); port 9090
[New] postscreen rule: 3 patterns for Postfix postscreen pre-filter (PREGREET,
      DNSBL rank, HANGUP); weight=1/trip=40 (noisy tier); port 25
[New] sshd rule: 4 new patterns for OpenSSH 7.6+/8.0+ (Connection closed by
      authenticating user, Disconnected from authenticating user, banner exchange,
      Unable to negotiate)
[New] postfix rule: 2 new patterns for connection-abuse detection (lost connection
      after AUTH, too many errors after AUTH)
[New] dovecot rule: ManageSieve auth failure pattern (managesieve-login), port 4190
[New] apache-auth rule: 2 new patterns for digest auth (AH01620/AH01621/AH01622)
      and AuthzDBD failures (AH02572)
[New] mongodb rule: 2 new patterns for MongoDB 4.4+ JSON structured log format
      (client field) and 6.0+ (remote field rename)
[New] postgresql rule: user enumeration pattern (role does not exist)
[New] openvpn rule: address-spoofing detection pattern (MULTI: bad source address)

-- Canonical elog_lib Upgrade --

[Change] elog_lib.sh upgraded to canonical v1.0.0 from elog_lib upstream: adds
      elog_init() log directory/file setup, elog_event() structured JSONL audit
      events, output module registry with source-filtered dispatch, periodic
      inode-preserving log truncation, elog_critical() wrapper, and logrotate
      snippet generator; existing elog() API fully backward-compatible
[New] elog_init() called in config_init() to initialize /var/log/bfd/ directory
      and audit.log; non-fatal on failure (app logging unaffected)
[New] ELOG_LOG_DIR, ELOG_AUDIT_FILE, ELOG_LOG_MAX_LINES config variables in
      internals.conf with safe defaults
[New] elog_event() structured audit events for block_added, block_removed,
      config_loaded, config_error, and service_state; written as JSONL to
      /var/log/bfd/audit.log with key=value metadata fields

-- Syslog Idle Suppression --

[New] LOG_IDLE_SUPPRESS config variable (default: 1) suppresses idle zero-event
      run-complete messages from syslog; BFD log file always records every cycle
[New] eout() "l" flag for log-file-only output (no syslog)

-- Fixes --

[Fix] internals.conf: augment PATH with /sbin:/usr/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/local/sbin
      to ensure firewall and utility binaries are discoverable under cron's minimal
      PATH; matches APF's internals.conf pattern
[Change] config_init: warn when firewall backend fails to initialize instead of
      silently continuing; prevents silent ban failures on misconfigured systems

-- Threat Activity --

[Change] --attackpool retained as silent alias; all user-facing text
      (help, man page, README, bash completion) switched to --activity
[Change] -e/--events descriptions updated from "pressure dashboard" to
      "active events" across help, man page, and README
[Change] bfd.1 man page: -a description updated for threat activity report,
      --activity alias, dual-interval summary layout, -a vs -e usage note;
      attack.pool FILES entry updated
[Change] README.md: section 5.3 renamed to Threat Activity; expanded report
      description with summary, dual-interval columns, -a vs -e comparison;
      CLI help snippet and state files table updated
[New] Expanded per-service threat breakdown: dual-interval columns (24h/7d)
      for count, unique IPs, and top country; replaces single-interval view
      in text, JSON, and CSV output
[Change] Threat activity report section order: summary, 24h IPs, 7d IPs,
      per-service breakdown (was: 24h, services, 7d); consistent across text,
      JSON, and CSV output formats
[New] Threat activity summary header: aggregate unique IPs (24h/7d), total
      count (24h/7d), and active bans shown at top of -a/--activity report;
      included in JSON (summary key) and CSV (# summary section)
[New] --activity alias for -a/--attackpool; user-facing labels renamed from
      "attack pool" / "brute force attackers" to "threat activity" / "threat IPs"

-- Email --

[Fix] HTML email: base64-encode HTML MIME part to comply with RFC 5321
      998-character line limit; fixes Exim rejection of long inline-CSS lines
[Change] EMAIL_LOGLINES default reduced from 50 to 5; events per-IP view
      (bfd -e IP) now shares this setting; optional count override via
      bfd -e IP N

-- Internal Library Reorganization --

[Change] Internal libraries (bfd.lib.sh, tlog_lib.sh, elog_lib.sh,
      alert_lib.sh, internals.conf) moved to internals/ subdirectory;
      reduces top-level clutter, simplifies library sourcing to single
      BASH_SOURCE-relative pattern; install.sh, importconf, packaging,
      and symlink farm updated for new layout

-- Template Overrides --

[New] Template overrides: alert/custom.d/ directory for per-file template
      customization that persists across upgrades; one-time auto-migration
      of previously modified templates; health check reports active overrides

-- Email Template Rebrand --

[Change] HTML email templates rebranded to rfxn.com design system: teal brand
      bar header with monospace rfxn logo and uppercase tagline, zinc neutrals,
      surface cards, pill badge count, severity top-line entry cards
[Change] Ban type severity colors: temporary teal (#0891b2), escalated amber
      (#d97706), permanent red (#dc2626)
[Change] Pressure bar colors: success green (#16a34a), warning amber (#d97706),
      critical red (#dc2626)

-- Pressure Trip Ceiling --

[New] Pressure trip ceiling (max 200): enforced in validate_config(),
      _load_pressure_conf(), and importconf TRIG migration; values above 200
      effectively disable detection under exponential decay
[Fix] importconf: TRIG values above 200 clamped during migration to
      PRESSURE_TRIP; old TRIG counted raw failures (different scale from
      pressure model); also clamps inherited PRESSURE_TRIP>200 post-merge

-- Per-Rule Pressure Trip Display --

[New] _resolve_trip()/_resolve_min_trip(): per-rule pressure trip threshold
      helpers; resolve from _PRESS_TRIP[] with GLOB_PRESSURE_TRIP fallback
[Change] Events dashboard/CIDR/per-IP, search_ip, and attack pool views now
      display per-rule pressure trip thresholds from pressure.conf instead of
      the global PRESSURE_TRIP default; aggregate views show the minimum
      per-rule trip across matched services

-- Test Alert --

[New] --test-alert email: send a test email alert to verify the full delivery
      pipeline (rendering, MIME, local MTA or SMTP relay) with synthetic data;
      requires EMAIL_ALERTS=1; honors EMAIL_FORMAT, SMTP_RELAY, and all email
      config; bypasses digest mode for immediate delivery

-- Watch Mode --

[Fix] Watch mode: suppress elog stdout in daemon mode to prevent duplicate
      syslog entries; systemd SyslogIdentifier captures stdout, creating a
      second entry alongside the direct syslog write from elog

-- Multi-Channel Alerting Documentation --

[Change] bfd.1 man page: Slack, Telegram, Discord configuration sections;
      --test-alert expanded with all channel types; Alert Templates section
      with messaging template reference
[Change] README.md: sections 3.11-3.13 for Slack, Telegram, Discord setup
      with config tables and quick-start examples; messaging template table
      in section 3.10
[Change] bfd.bash-completion: --test-alert completions expanded with slack,
      telegram, discord; config variable completions updated with messaging
      and SMTP variables

-- Multi-Channel Alerting --

[New] Multi-channel alerting: Slack (webhook and Bot API), Telegram (Bot API),
      and Discord (webhook) alert delivery via shared alert_lib channel
      registry; configurable per-channel in conf.bfd
[New] conf.bfd: SLACK_ALERTS, SLACK_MODE, SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, SLACK_TOKEN,
      SLACK_CHANNEL, TELEGRAM_ALERTS, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID,
      DISCORD_ALERTS, DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL with conservative defaults (disabled)
[New] Messaging templates: Block Kit JSON (Slack), MarkdownV2 (Telegram),
      embed JSON (Discord) with per-entry ban details and summary footer
[New] --test-alert slack|telegram|discord: send test alerts to verify
      messaging channel configuration and delivery pipeline
[Change] Health check (-c): validates messaging channel config — curl
      presence, required credentials/URLs per channel and mode
[Change] show_config (-C): messaging variables added to whitelist
[Change] Digest flush respects messaging channels — spool flushes when any
      alert channel is enabled, not just EMAIL_ALERTS

-- Shared Alert Library Integration --

[Change] Alert subsystem refactored: generic primitives (template engine, MIME
      builder, email delivery, digest/spool) replaced with shared alert_lib
      v1.0.0; BFD-specific functions (content helpers, rendering pipeline,
      data preparation) extracted to bfd_alert.sh
[Change] Digest wrappers (_bfd_spool_append, _bfd_digest_check, _bfd_digest_flush)
      bridge BFD config variables to shared alert_lib's explicit-argument API
[Change] Email delivery variables (SMTP_*) mapped to shared library env vars
      (ALERT_SMTP_*) via _bfd_alert_init() at config initialization

-- SMTP Relay Fixes --

[Fix] _alert_send_relay(): --ssl-reqd was applied unconditionally, breaking
      smtp://host:25 plain connections for internal relays; now conditional on
      URL scheme (smtps:// and smtp://:587 require TLS, smtp://:25 is plain)
[Fix] _alert_send_relay(): SMTP credentials were required as hard error,
      preventing auth-free internal relays; now optional (--user flag omitted
      when SMTP_USER/SMTP_PASS are empty)
[Fix] _alert_send_relay(): curl stderr was suppressed with 2>/dev/null; now
      captured to temp file and included in elog error message on failure

-- Log Sample Pattern Filtering --

[New] _events_rule_patterns(): extract detection patterns from rule files by
      sourcing in subshell with pattern-capturing extract_hosts() override
[Change] _alert_sanitize_logs(): accept optional detection patterns parameter;
      when provided, filters log lines by rule patterns instead of blanket IP grep
[Change] events_ip()/events_ip_json(): pass rule patterns to log sample extraction
      so only failure lines matching detection rules are shown
[Change] _alert_set_entry_vars(): pass service patterns to log sample for email
      alerts, filtering out non-failure log entries

-- Alert Integration Tests --

[New] Integration tests for email pipeline: check() digest spool path, multi-cycle
      accumulation, SKIP_ALERT filtering, RULE_EMAIL routing through digest,
      timing-based digest flush via mail, scan-mode force-flush, relay delivery
      from digest, MIME structure validation for format=both, watch mode digest
      flush on shutdown, cron.daily stale spool truncation and fresh preservation

-- Alert Documentation --

[Change] bfd.1 man page: EMAIL_FORMAT, EMAIL_DIGEST, SMTP relay variables in
      config section; new Email Templates and SMTP Relay subsections;
      alert.bfd replaced by alert_lib.sh + alert/ in FILES section
[Change] README.md: section 3.2 expanded with EMAIL_FORMAT, EMAIL_DIGEST,
      EMAIL_REPUTATION_LINKS; new sections 3.9 (SMTP Relay) and 3.10
      (Email Templates) with variable reference and customization guide

-- Alert Packaging --

[Change] install.sh: alert.bfd replaced by alert_lib.sh (chmod 640) and
      alert/ template directory (chmod 750, templates 640)
[Change] importconf: preserve user-customized alert/ templates on upgrade;
      legacy alert.bfd preserved for pre-2.0.1 upgrades
[Change] RPM spec: alert.bfd replaced by alert_lib.sh + alert/ directory in
      %build path transforms, %install, %files, and symlink farm
[Change] DEB rules/links: alert.bfd replaced by alert_lib.sh + alert/ directory
      in install targets and backward-compat symlinks
[Change] pkg test: alert.bfd checks replaced by alert_lib.sh + alert/ directory
      + ALERT_TEMPLATE_DIR FHS path + template file count verification

-- Alert Configuration --

[New] conf.bfd: EMAIL_FORMAT, EMAIL_DIGEST, EMAIL_DIGEST_INTERVAL,
      EMAIL_REPUTATION_LINKS, SMTP_RELAY, SMTP_FROM, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS
      variables with conservative defaults matching existing behavior
[Change] validate_config(): EMAIL_FORMAT/DIGEST enum validation, SMTP_RELAY URL
      format check, SMTP_FROM required + email validation, reputation links
      known-provider check (warning), SMTP credentials warning
[Change] _hc_alerts(): expanded health checks — sendmail for html/both format,
      curl for SMTP relay, SMTP_FROM/credentials, alert template directory and
      all 8 template partials presence
[Change] show_config(): whitelist extended with EMAIL_FORMAT, EMAIL_DIGEST,
      EMAIL_DIGEST_INTERVAL, EMAIL_REPUTATION_LINKS, SMTP_RELAY, SMTP_FROM,
      ALERT_TEMPLATE_DIR, APOOL_RETENTION_DAYS, APOOL_MAX_LINES

-- Attack Pool --

[Change] state_pool_append(): enriched 10-field format — TIMESTAMP IP MOD
      COUNT CC ACTION DURATION PORTS PRESSURE TRIP_TYPE; backward compatible
      with old 3-field entries (COUNT=1, CC=--, ACTION=ban, etc.)
[Change] check(): restructure pool write path — append moves after ban outcome
      to capture action, duration, and trip type; country lookup via warm cache
[Change] check_distributed(): pass enriched fields (unique_count, ban_action,
      duration, trip_type=subnet) to state_pool_append
[Change] _apool_awk(): sum $4 count field, extract $5 country code
[Change] _apool_service_summary_awk(): sum $4 count field for per-service totals
[Change] _apool_report()/json/csv: add COUNTRY column/key to output
[New] state_pool_prune(): age-based pruning with max-lines safety cap,
      mirrors state_events_prune() pattern with flock + inode-preserving rewrite
[New] conf.bfd: APOOL_RETENTION_DAYS (default 365), APOOL_MAX_LINES (default 500000)
[Change] cron.daily: age-based pruning replaces daily rotation; one-time
      migration consolidates existing .MMDDYY.HHMM archives into single pool
[Change] check(): periodic pool pruning in watch mode (24h marker-based timer)
[Change] _apool_awk()/_apool_service_summary_awk(): add cutoff parameter for
      timestamp-based filtering (early AWK skip — no memory for old entries)
[Change] apool_list()/json/csv: timestamp-based "Last 24h" / "Last 7d" views
      replace file-based "today" / "this week" — no temp files needed
[Change] search_ip()/json/csv: enriched pool display showing failure count
      + ban count (attack_pool_failures + attack_pool_triggers)
[Remove] _apool_prepare_weekly(): eliminated (timestamp filtering replaces
      find+cat of fragmented archive files)

-- Reporting --

[Change] Rename EVENTS column/key to COUNT across all text/JSON/CSV views:
      attack pool, events dashboard, events per-IP, events CIDR, search_ip
[Change] search_ip: "Events (24h)" label renamed to "Failures (24h)";
      events_24h key renamed to count_24h in JSON/CSV output
[Change] events_cidr: total_events key renamed to total_count in JSON;
      summary line uses "failures" instead of "events"

-- Events Per-IP --

[New] _events_rule_log_file(): extract LOG_FILE from rule without triggering
      detection (subshell with _rule_tlog/extract_hosts no-op override)
[Change] events_ip(): append "Recent log activity" section, up to 15 sanitized
      log lines via _alert_sanitize_logs(), deduplicating shared log files
[Change] events_ip_json(): add log_sample string array to JSON output

-- CLI --

[Change] usage_short(): add compact CLI matrix line listing all flags in
      [-x|--long] form; expand common commands by category with brief
      descriptions matching LMD's usage output style

-- Alert Digest --

[New] _alert_spool_append(): append timestamped entries to digest spool under
      flock for timed accumulation across detection cycles
[New] _alert_digest_check(): flush spool when EMAIL_DIGEST_INTERVAL expires;
      optimistic age check without lock, flush under exclusive flock
[New] _alert_digest_flush_now(): force-send accumulated alerts, strip epoch
      prefix, truncate spool; releases lock before SMTP delivery
[Change] check(): conditional spool vs immediate send based on EMAIL_DIGEST
      mode; digest check runs every cycle for pre-existing spool entries
[Change] cleanup_watch(): flush digest spool before watch mode shutdown
[Change] config_init(): unset EMAIL_FORMAT, EMAIL_DIGEST, EMAIL_DIGEST_INTERVAL,
      EMAIL_REPUTATION_LINKS, SMTP_RELAY/USER/PASS/FROM on reload
[Change] --scan: force-flush digest spool after scan completion
[Change] cron.daily: safety truncation for stale digest spool (>24h)

-- Alert Delivery --

[New] _alert_send_local(): local MTA delivery with text/html/multipart format
      support; sendmail fallback to text-only via mail when unavailable
[New] _alert_send_relay(): authenticated SMTP relay delivery via curl with
      --ssl-reqd, credential validation, and error reporting
[New] _alert_send(): delivery router between local MTA and SMTP relay; relay
      path always builds full multipart MIME for richest content
[Change] send_alerts() rewritten to use template-based rendering pipeline and
      structured delivery functions; drops legacy sourced-template approach
[Change] EMAIL_FORMAT support: text (default), html, both (multipart/alternative)
[Change] SMTP relay support: configurable via SMTP_RELAY, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS,
      SMTP_FROM variables
[Change] ALERT_TEMPLATE_DIR replaces EMAIL_TEMPLATE in internals.conf; points to
      files/alert/ template partials directory

-- New Features --

[New] Alert rendering pipeline: data preparation (_alert_set_global_vars,
      _alert_set_entry_vars), summary aggregation (_alert_compute_summary),
      text and HTML render orchestrators (_alert_render_text, _alert_render_html),
      multipart/alternative MIME construction (_alert_build_mime); per-entry
      variables include pressure bar, ban type colors, country lookup, reputation
      links, history/escalation lines, sanitized source logs — all pre-computed
      for zero-logic template rendering
[Change] Alert template footer URLs updated to rfxn.com/projects/brute-force-detection
[New] Alert template partials (files/alert/): 8 customizable {{VAR}} templates
      (4 plain text + 4 HTML) replacing sourced-bash alert.bfd; email-safe HTML
      with inline CSS and table layout; self-contained entry/summary cards;
      conditional sections via pre-computed variables for zero-logic templates
[New] Alert engine library (alert_lib.sh): safe {{VAR}} template renderer via
      awk ENVIRON substitution (no shell sourcing), HTML entity escaping,
      credential-redacting log sanitizer, IP reputation link builder
      (AbuseIPDB, Shodan, VirusTotal, IPinfo, GreyNoise), ASCII pressure bar
      visualization, color helpers for ban severity and pressure level,
      Unicode country flag emoji from 2-letter codes
[New] Pressure-to-response scoring model: exponential-decay scoring replaces
      fixed count thresholds; events add weighted pressure per rule, pressure
      decays via configurable half-life, bans fire when accumulated pressure
      exceeds trip point; cross-service aggregate trip; all math in native awk
      floats; old TRIG/TRIG_WINDOW configs auto-migrate
[New] Country pressure multipliers: auto-enabled when pressure-country.conf has
      entries; IP-to-country lookup via ipcountry.dat binary search;
      pressure-country.conf maps country codes to multipliers
[New] Per-rule pressure configuration via pressure.conf: PRESSURE_WEIGHT,
      PRESSURE_TRIP, SKIP_ALERT, RULE_EMAIL with three-tier precedence
      (rule file > pressure.conf > conf.bfd)
[New] Watch mode (-w/--watch): continuous daemon with configurable interval;
      SIGHUP config reload; systemd unit and SysVinit init script; dead-PID
      lock recovery for cron fallback
[New] Scan mode (--scan): full-log processing for all rules or a specific rule;
      supports dry-run, --max-lines=N, --scan-timeout=N; SCAN_MAX_LINES and
      SCAN_TIMEOUT config variables with startup validation
[New] Events CLI (--events): active pressure dashboard showing all tracked IPs
      with pressure scores, event counts, services, and ban proximity;
      per-IP detail with per-service breakdown; CIDR subnet reports;
      --json/--csv structured output for all modes
[New] Structured output (--json/--csv) for ban list (-l), events dashboard
      (-e), and attack pool reports (-a) including per-service breakdowns
      and unified IP reports
[New] FIREWALL="auto" with 8 backends: APF, CSF, firewalld, UFW, nftables,
      iptables, route, custom; auto-detection in priority order; nftables
      sets, iptables chain, firewalld rich rules, route blackhole
[New] Full IPv6 support: dual-stack detection, banning, and local address
      exclusion; BAN_COMMAND_V6/UNBAN_COMMAND_V6 for firewalls requiring
      separate commands
[New] Temporary bans with auto-expiry (BAN_TTL); recidivism escalation
      (BAN_ESCALATE_AFTER/BAN_ESCALATE_WINDOW); escalation modes
      (none/linear/double with configurable cap); retry with exponential
      backoff; old names (BAN_DURATION, BAN_PERMANENT_AFTER/WINDOW) accepted
[New] Distributed attack detection: SUBNET_TRIG unique IPs from same subnet
      triggers subnet ban; configurable IPv4/IPv6 masks
[New] Batched email alerts: single email per recipient per check cycle with
      enriched content (ban type, duration, recidivism, log excerpts);
      per-rule routing and suppression via RULE_EMAIL/SKIP_ALERT; atomic
      state file appends via flock; port-specific blocking via $PORTS
[New] Declarative rule engine with fail2ban-compatible <HOST> patterns,
      dual IPv4/IPv6 boundary-aware regex, and IGNOREREGEX per-rule exclusion;
      all rules converted from ad-hoc grep/sed/awk pipelines
[New] 22 new service rules (42 total): apache-auth, nginx-http-auth,
      mysqld-auth, wordpress, webmin, directadmin, cyrus-imap, roundcube,
      plesk, dropbear, http_401, pam_generic, named, postgresql,
      openvpn, phpmyadmin, gitlab, grafana, proxmox, lighttpd, mongodb, xrdp
[New] In-process tlog wrapper replaces external subprocess calls in all rules;
      eliminates fork+exec pairs per detection cycle
[New] Systemd journal reader with transparent fallback (16 of 34 rules);
      LOG_SOURCE config (auto/file/journal); cursor-based journal tracking;
      23 service-to-journalctl filter mappings via dynamic registry
[New] tlog_lib.sh shared incremental log reader: atomic cursor writes, optional
      flock-based locking, cursor validation with auto-reset, stale cursor
      protection, configurable first-run behavior, multi-format compressed
      rotation support, copytruncate handling, and generic decompression
[New] elog_lib.sh structured logging library with severity levels, classic
      syslog-style and JSON output formats, configurable via LOG_FORMAT and
      LOG_LEVEL
[New] CLI expanded from 4 to 21 flags: -S/--status, -C/--config, -R/--rules,
      -T/--test, --test-pattern, -l/--list, -u/--unban, -b/--ban, -c/--check,
      -d/--dryrun, -w/--watch, -V/--verbose, -v/--version, -h/--help,
      --flush-temp, --flush-all, --json, --csv
[New] Health check (-c/--check): validates config, log paths, firewall
      binaries, rule status, state directories, tlog, and active bans
[New] Run mode detection: structured identification (watch/systemd, watch/init,
      watch/manual, timer/systemd, cron, unknown)
[New] Verbose mode (-V/--verbose): per-IP pressure score, trip threshold,
      effective weight, and country multiplier shown during detection cycles
[New] Short and full help output: common commands shown with no arguments,
      full help via -h with semantic section grouping and examples
[New] bfd.1 nroff man page: OPTIONS, CONFIGURATION, PRESSURE MODEL, FIREWALL,
      RULES, FILES, SIGNALS, EXIT CODES; scan mode, events, structured output,
      upgrade guide
[New] bfd.bash-completion: context-sensitive tab completion for all CLI flags,
      IPs, rule names, config variables, and file paths
[New] importconf rewritten: awk-based config merge preserving user values;
      TRIG to PRESSURE_TRIP migration; thresholds.conf to pressure.conf
      per-rule translation; pre-2.0.1 backward compat; temp file cleanup trap
[New] install.sh: custom paths via INSTALL_PATH/BIN_PATH env vars; man page,
      bash completion, and SysVinit init script installation; auto-enable
      watch mode on fresh install; upgrade notice for watch mode on v1.5
      upgrades
[New] uninstall.sh: root check; service stop ordering; man page, completion,
      init script, backup directory, and custom log path cleanup
[New] Security functions: safe_source() validates ownership and permissions
      before sourcing; safe template expansion without eval; strict IP and
      email validation; rule name sanitization
[New] Per-cycle caching: ignore file merge for fast per-IP lookup; country
      lookup cache; pre-computed IP occurrence counts; timestamp formatting
      helpers replacing 30 inline date fallback patterns
[New] systemd units: bfd.service, bfd.timer, bfd-watch.service with
      SyslogIdentifier
[New] RPM packaging: FHS-compliant layout (/usr/sbin, /usr/lib/bfd, /etc/bfd,
      /usr/share/bfd, /var/lib/bfd); symlink farm at /usr/local/bfd for
      backward compat; sed transforms at build time; config(noreplace) for
      user-editable config; SysVinit service handling in scriptlets; single
      spec covers el7/el8/el9/el10
[New] DEB packaging: FHS layout with dh_link-based symlink farm;
      debhelper-compat 13; conffile protection; SysVinit init script included;
      install.sh-to-package migration; single .deb covers Debian 12 and
      Ubuntu 18/20/22/24
[New] Package build infrastructure: source tarball via git archive; native
      rpm/deb targets; Docker build containers for el7, el9, and Debian 12;
      10-category verification test suite covering FHS paths, symlink farm,
      config transforms, permissions, rule files, systemd units, and execution
[New] GitHub Actions release workflow: builds RPM (el7/el8/el9/el10) and DEB
      packages in parallel on tag push; creates GitHub Release with assets;
      build jobs gated by tag-push guard to prevent wasted CI on dispatch
[New] GitHub Actions CI pipeline: 10-OS Docker matrix with Buildx caching,
      bash -n syntax checks, and shellcheck static analysis; DEB maintainer
      scripts and bash-completion included in lint targets
[New] BATS test suite: 1200 tests across 36 files; shared helpers; parallel
      runner; 10 Dockerfiles; RFC 5737 test IPs; dedicated pressure model,
      country multiplier, watch mode, and scan mode test suites

-- Bug Fixes --

[Fix] Security: alert eval echo injection replaced with safe template
      expansion; show_config() eval injection guarded by whitelist;
      BAN_COMMAND template extracted raw preventing premature expansion;
      custom backend PORTS validated
[Fix] Security: safe_source() applied to all sourced files; state file
      operations wrapped in flock; mktemp replaces PID-based temp files;
      tlog gunzip/gzip race replaced with zcat
[Fix] Security: reject group-writable files in addition to world-writable
      in file safety checks; sanitize credential patterns in alert email
      log excerpts; validate IGNOREREGEX patterns before use
[Fix] Global lock: FD-based flock replaced with mkdir-based lock eliminating
      eval and fd-0-close risk; PID liveness check clears dead holder
      immediately for cron recovery
[Fix] Watch mode: SIGTERM/SIGINT now properly exit the daemon; previous trap
      pattern let the while-true loop continue after cleanup
[Fix] Watch mode reload: unset config vars BEFORE re-sourcing to prevent
      stale values; clear pressure arrays; re-register journal filters on
      SIGHUP; re-derive log format variables; add fallback variable block
      for config-sourcing failures; pre-validate syntax and permissions
      before unsetting to prevent degraded daemon state
[Fix] Watch mode reload: config validation uses return instead of exit,
      preventing daemon crash on validation errors
[Fix] Upgrade path: importconf preserves pressure-country.conf, custom rule
      files, exclude.files, custom alert.bfd template, tlog cursor state
      files, and user-customized cron schedule on upgrade
[Fix] Upgrade path: health check validates UNBAN_COMMAND and UNBAN_COMMAND_V6
      binary existence
[Fix] install.sh: stop watch mode before upgrade to avoid restart delay;
      daemon-reload after sed; BINPATH parent dir creation; CWD portability;
      set sourced libraries to 640 permissions; chmod 750 on install directory;
      update-ipcountry.sh set executable and added to path replacement list
[Fix] nftables status: count actual set elements instead of reporting 1
      regardless of element count
[Fix] cron.daily: use dedicated lock file for flock to avoid write contention;
      check mkdir-based lock before rotating state files to prevent racing
      with running bfd process
[Fix] JSON escape: newline, tab, CR, backspace, and formfeed per RFC 8259;
      previously only backslash and double-quote were escaped
[Fix] Attack pool dedup: exact matching for rule names; previous substring
      match falsely deduped vsftpd/vsftpd2 and openvpn/openvpnas pairs
[Fix] Config validation: added OUTPUT_SYSLOG, EMAIL_ADDRESS, BFD_LOG_PATH,
      BAN_RETRY_COUNT, EMAIL_LOGLINES, LOG_FORMAT, LOG_LEVEL, and
      SCAN_TIMEOUT=0 validation; BAN_ESCALATION error mentions "exponential"
      as accepted deprecated alias
[Fix] show_config(): replace eval-based variable indirection with indirect
      expansion; BAN_COMMAND vars added to whitelist
[Fix] Rule variable leakage: IGNOREREGEX/PORTS/SKIP_ALERT/RULE_EMAIL now
      properly reset between rules via save/restore/clear helpers
[Fix] CLI exit codes: all dispatch branches validate args and propagate
      correctly; unknown flags exit non-zero
[Fix] Firewall backends: hardcoded paths replaced with command -v discovery;
      CIDR addresses pass through without extra suffix; guard against empty
      ip6tables binary with warning
[Fix] Symlink handling: stat -c calls add -L flag to dereference symlinks
      for package installs where files are symlinks to FHS locations
[Fix] Quiet mode (-q): remove stderr redirect so genuine errors reach cron's
      mail handler; stdout suppression sufficient for cron silence
[Fix] tlog: log rotation duplicate output; source safety validation; BASERUN
      install-time path replacement prevents cursor files in /tmp; unquote
      journal filter for multi-filter entries
[Fix] State files: restore 600 permissions after awk rewrite temp file;
      enforce 750 permissions on tmp/ and stats/ directories; log file
      creation uses chmod 640 to match logrotate directive
[Fix] Pressure alerts: format_alert_body read 11 fields from 12-field alert
      file corrupting email display; ATTACK_COUNT backward compat now uses
      pressure/1000 for sensible old-template display
[Fix] Display: status rounding normalized to match pressure computation;
      5 display functions used hardcoded trip default of 15 instead of 20
[Fix] Rule status: backward-compat variable mapping now called after sourcing
      rule files so old-style rules are counted correctly
[Fix] Ignore files: inline comments after IPs now handled correctly
[Fix] Subnet detection: defensive guard for masks below /8
[Fix] Pressure config: PRESSURE_WEIGHT and PRESSURE_TRIP values type-validated;
      non-numeric or zero values logged and skipped
[Fix] Rule fixes: postgresql impossible path test; vsftpd2 tag collision;
      modsec variable rename; missing SKIP_ALERT in postfix/proftpd;
      ignore.hosts missing ::1 loopback
[Fix] IPv6: grep false-match replaced with exact matching
[Fix] Journal: filter key mismatch for rh_ipop3d; dispatch bypassed existing
      log files
[Fix] Tab completion: config_vars updated from old variable names to match
      current config whitelist
[Fix] Packaging: add tlog_lib.sh and elog_lib.sh to RPM spec and DEB
      manifests; add SysVinit service stop and deregister to all scriptlets
[Fix] Miscellaneous: POSIX == to = in test brackets; exit code quoting;
      attack pool regex to fixed-string grep; local address grep fix;
      WATCH_INTERVAL default syntax; sed -r to sed -E; UNBAN_COMMAND warning
      gated on FIREWALL="custom"; firewalld examples removed --permanent flag

-- Changes --

[Change] conf.bfd restructured into workflow-oriented sections (Pressure Model,
      Email Alerts, Banning, Custom Firewall Commands, Log Paths, Advanced);
      comments rewritten with worked examples; BAN_ESCALATION "exponential"
      renamed to "double" (old value still accepted); 4 internal-only
      variables moved to internals.conf; new variables documented as
      commented entries for discoverability
[Change] check() rewritten: pressure-based scoring replaces count-based
      thresholds; per-rule weight/trip/half-life; optional country multipliers;
      global cross-service pressure trip; per-run statistics;
      duplicate-ban prevention; per-cycle caching for country lookups and
      ignore lists; pre-computed IP occurrence counts
[Change] Rule variables renamed for clarity: REQ to PREREQ, LP to LOG_FILE,
      TLOG_TF to LOG_TAG, ARG_VAL to MATCHED_HOSTS; backward-compat shim
      for custom rules using old names
[Change] Rule validation rewritten to distinguish inactive rules from genuine
      misconfigurations; detection output now verbose-only with summary format
[Change] weights.country renamed to pressure-country.conf; PRESSURE_COUNTRY
      toggle removed in favor of auto-detection
[Change] Extract shared config_init() for startup and reload, eliminating
      duplicated config loading logic
[Change] Extract shared helpers: cleanup teardown, firewall retry with
      exponential backoff, file safety validation, pressure aggregation,
      events AWK processing
[Change] Structured output refactor: shared data helpers for ban list, attack
      pool, events, and IP search; each format (text/JSON/CSV) shares a
      single data source instead of reading state files multiple times
[Change] Logging: eout()/vout() rewritten as thin wrappers delegating to elog
      library; log calls assigned explicit severity levels; error and warning
      messages now write to stderr per UNIX convention
[Change] Email validation for addresses in config and per-rule RULE_EMAIL
[Change] importconf: defense-in-depth integer validation on legacy variable
      migrations and per-rule config values
[Change] tlog CLI rewritten with option parsing, subcommands, help system,
      path traversal rejection, and library security validation;
      backward-compatible positional interface preserved
[Change] tlog_lib.sh updated to canonical 2.0.2: rotation refactored with
      pipe fallback for disk-full; journal flock support; cursor validation
      hardening; CLI version cross-check
[Change] Shell modernization across all files: backticks to $(), $[expr] to
      $(( )), egrep to grep -E, for-cat to while-read, systematic variable
      quoting, hardcoded paths to command -v discovery
[Change] Remove dead deprecated functions and unused variables
[Change] sshd rule expanded from 3 to 8 patterns: keyboard-interactive, ident
      string, refused connect, max auth attempts, PAM failure
[Change] dovecot rule expanded from 2 to 5 patterns: Disconnected pop3/imap,
      submission-login auth failed; AUTH_LOG_PATH fallback for Debian/Ubuntu
[Change] proftpd rule expanded from 1 to 4 patterns: incorrect password,
      SECURITY VIOLATION, maximum login attempts
[Change] exim rules: expanded patterns, Debian support with exim4 binary and
      log path fallbacks
[Change] asterisk rules: SecurityEvent FailedACL pattern added; log path
      fallback for /var/log/asterisk/messages
[Change] postfix PORTS updated from 25,26 to 25,26,587,465 (submission/SMTPS)
[Change] sendmail rule expanded from 1 to 2 patterns: AUTH failure
[Change] http_401 and pam_generic rules: conservative defaults to prevent
      false positives
[Change] Attack pool (-a) extended with IP search report, per-service
      breakdown, ban status integration, and pressure column in top-25 reports
[Change] update-ipcountry.sh: download timeout, TLS fallback for legacy CA
      bundles, temp files in install path
[Change] install.sh: contextual progress output for every blocking stage;
      stage markers and summary block
[Change] UFW backend: comment marker on deny rules for identification;
      graceful fallback for older versions; status reports deny rule count
[Change] logrotate rewritten: copytruncate, weekly, compress, create 0640
[Change] cron.daily: flock-wrapped state rotation; copy-and-truncate preserves
      inodes; cursor files preserved; GPL header added
[Change] Default cron interval reduced from 3 to 2 minutes
[Change] README wholesale rewrite: quick start, config reference, rule catalog,
      ban lifecycle, firewall backends, IPv6, CLI flags, scan mode, events
      dashboard, structured output, upgrade guide, troubleshooting
[Change] Version 1.6-1 to 2.0.1; copyright years updated to 2026
